    "claim": "Process lesson (bit three times, 2026-08-16): killing processes by pattern match kills your own shell - the bash -c command text contains the pattern. And `cd X && nohup python ... &` backgrounds the whole list, so $! is the SUBSHELL pid, not pythons - pid files written that way lie, and kill $(cat pidfile) silently no-ops after the subshell exits. Reliable: scan /proc matching the executable path in cmdline[0] plus an argument, excluding os.getpid(); or write the pidfile from INSIDE the nohup-ed script ($$).",
